# Recent-Deals Benchmark Golden Dataset

Use this rule when editing `tests/golden/recent-deals-benchmark.json`, benchmark
validators, or the gate script. Keep scaffold samples structurally valid while
`placeholder` is true. Treat gate readiness as a separate, stricter bar.

## Validation Modes

- `validateBenchmarkScaffold(raw)` in
  `packages/domain/src/benchmark/recent-deals-benchmark-validation.ts`
  checks root keys (`placeholder`, `rows` only), row shape, nested objects,
  enums, and formats. Placeholder datasets must still pass so CI catches typos
  early.
- `validateBenchmarkGateReady(raw, options?)` runs scaffold validation, then
  enforces coverage gate rules. It returns `ok: false` when `placeholder` is
  `true` with an explicit Task 1.2 style message.

## Gate-Ready Requirements

Gate-ready means all of the following, in addition to scaffold shape:

- `placeholder` must be `false`. `"placeholder": true` is intentionally not
  gate-ready even if rows look realistic.
- Between 20 and 30 rows inclusive (`GATE_MIN_ROWS` / `GATE_MAX_ROWS` in the
  validator implementation).
- Each `discovered_date` must be a valid `YYYY-MM-DD` calendar date in UTC,
  within the last 90 days relative to validation time (`now`, defaulting to
  runtime `Date`), not in the future.
- Each `source_url` must parse as HTTPS. Hostnames must not match blocked
  reserved or private ranges (including `example.*`, `localhost`, loopback,
  RFC1918-style IPv4, documented IPv6 documentation and ULA prefixes, and
  similar cases implemented in `findBlockedUrlHostname`).
- String fields across each row are scanned for PII-shaped email tokens,
  including percent-encoded and nested JSON string values (see
  `collectJsonStrings`, `decodeURIComponent`, and
  `decodeValidPercentTriplets` in the reference implementation).
- `source_site` must not be the scaffold sentinel `sample-source`.

## Command

- Run `pnpm benchmark:gate` from the repo root. It executes
  `tsx scripts/validate-recent-deals-benchmark.ts`, which reads
  `tests/golden/recent-deals-benchmark.json` and calls
  `validateBenchmarkGateReady`. Non-zero exit means the file is not gate-ready.

## Pitfalls

- Fixing row shape while leaving `placeholder: true` still fails the gate.
  Update docs and plan status only after the gate passes.
- `discovered_date` lookback is tied to validation `now`. Tests may inject
  `options.now` so snapshots stay stable; the CLI uses real wall clock.
- `source_url` must be `https:` only; `http:` is rejected even for public hosts.
- Email-like tokens can hide under encoding (`%40`, double-encoded `%2540`).
  Prefer neutral placeholders in narrative fields.
- Extra keys on the root object or on rows fail scaffold validation before any
  gate-specific checks run.

## Reference Implementation Paths

- `packages/domain/src/benchmark/recent-deals-benchmark-validation.ts`:
  `validateBenchmarkScaffold`, `validateBenchmarkGateReady`, URL and PII
  helpers.
- `packages/domain/src/benchmark/recent-deals-benchmark-validation.test.ts`:
  unit coverage for both modes.
- `scripts/validate-recent-deals-benchmark.ts`: production gate entrypoint
  wired to `pnpm benchmark:gate`.
